/T (Most of this work targets large natural photographs and compares against a handful of rivals. Small, centred objects, impulse noise next to Gaussian noise, and the question of what happens when the input is only lightly corrupted get much less attention. This paper looks at exactly those cases, using a deliberately small experiment that anyone can rerun.)
/E (Most of this work targets large natural photographs and compares against a handful of rivals. Small, centred objects, impulse noise next to Gaussian noise, and the question of what happens when the input is only lightly corrupted get much less attention. This paper looks at exactly those cases, using a deliberately small experiment that anyone can rerun.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
