/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 39 0 R
/T (The results suggest a simple rule of thumb. If the noise is known to be light and Gaussian, a tuned bilateral filter is hard to beat and needs no training. If it is impulsive, a median filter is a sound and cheap choice. If the noise type or level is unknown or strong, a single trained CDAE is the safer bet, because it gave the best SSIM everywhere and the best PSNR in three of five conditions without being told which noise it faced.)
/E (The results suggest a simple rule of thumb. If the noise is known to be light and Gaussian, a tuned bilateral filter is hard to beat and needs no training. If it is impulsive, a median filter is a sound and cheap choice. If the noise type or level is unknown or strong, a single trained CDAE is the safer bet, because it gave the best SSIM everywhere and the best PSNR in three of five conditions without being told which noise it faced.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
