470 0 obj
<<
/Title (The results suggest a simple rule of thumb. If the noise is known to be light and Gaussian, a tuned bilateral filter is hard to beat and needs no training. If it is impulsive, a median filter is a sound and cheap choice. If the noise type or level is unknown or strong, a single trained CDAE is the safer bet, because it gave the best SSIM everywhere and the best PSNR in three of five conditions without being told which noise it faced.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 428 0 R
/Prev 462 0 R
/Next 478 0 R
>>
endobj
