484 0 obj
<<
/Title (Impulse noise: Among the classical methods the median filter is clearly the best \(20.87 dB and 20.05 dB\), which makes sense for outliers that sit at the extremes of the intensity range. The bilateral filter barely beats doing nothing \(17.44 dB and 14.70 dB, against 17.08 dB and 14.10 dB for the input\). A salt or pepper pixel differs so much from its neighbours that the range weight reads it as an edge and keeps it. The CDAE reaches 23.37 dB and 21.97 dB, which is 2.50 dB and 1.92 dB above the median filter, with the highest SSIM as well.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 444 0 R
/Prev 489 0 R
/First 490 0 R
/Last 491 0 R
/Count -2
/Next 477 0 R
>>
